%
(rs274ngc-quirks.ngc)
(Structural and lexical edge cases, composed to the NIST RS274/NGC line format: optional)
(block delete, optional line number, words/parameters/comments in any order, case)
(insensitive and whitespace-insignificant outside comments. NOT captured from any)
(application. Line endings are CRLF, which is a legal end-of-line marker.)

/N10 G21 G90 (block delete: this line is skipped when block-delete mode is on)
N10 G17 G21 G90 G94 (line numbers may be skipped and need not be in order)
N40 G0 X0 Y0
N50 g1 x10 y0 f1000 (input is case insensitive outside comments)
n55 x0 y10 (lowercase line number, and modal motion with no G word at all)
N60 x0 y0 (modal motion continues)
N70 S100(set speed)F200(feed) (a comment may sit between two words)
N80 (a semicolon inside parentheses does not start a comment ;) G0 X1 Y1
N90 (first comment) G4 P0.1 (second comment: only the last comment on a line is used)
N100 G0X +0. 12 34Y 7 (whitespace may appear inside a number: this is exactly G0 X+0.1234 Y7)
N120 G0 X.5 Y-.5 (no leading zero, negative, no trailing zeros)
N130 G1 X00.7500 Y+1 (leading and trailing zeros are not significant)
N140 M2 (program end: no line after this one is read at all)
N150 G0 X999 Y999 (must NOT be executed - it is past the program end)
%
this text follows the second percent sign and is not evaluated
